{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You led</b> — According to Rabbi Moses [ibn Janach]: at the time of crossing the sea, like the way of cattle going down into a valley. And it is possible: upon their resting in the wilderness, like 'You led with Your kindness' [Psalms]. And Moses and Aaron are the ones who brought the people out of Egypt, and Moses before Aaron because of the greatness of his prophetic rank."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:51.115464902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}